[7.429567, "o", "Analyze Caddy v2 access logs with anomaly detection.\r\n\r\nSources:\r\n  /path/to/file          Local file (supports glob patterns)\r\n  -                      Stdin (pipe)\r\n  docker://container     Docker container\r\n  k8s://pod              Kubernetes pod  (-n namespace)\r\n  journalctl://unit      systemd unit\r\n\r\nSubcommands:\r\n  tail [source...]       Colorized real-time log viewer\r\n  top <dimension>        Quick top-N metric inspector (path, ip, ua, status, bandwidth)\r\n  diff <log1> <log2>     Compare two log files for RPS shifts, 5xx spikes, and latency changes\r\n\r\nFiltering (activate colored log listing instead of report):\r\n  --ip <ip/CIDR>         Filter by client IP or subnet\r\n  -s, --status <codes>   Filter by HTTP status code(s)\r\n  -m, --method <verb>    Filter by HTTP method\r\n  -p, --path <glob>      Filter by request path (glob pattern)\r\n  --slow <duration>      Filter requests slower than duration\r\n  --2xx..--5xx           Filter by status class\r\n  -e, --errors-only      Filter server errors only\r\n  --no-bots / --bots-only Filter by traffic type\r\n  -g, --grep <pattern>   Search across URI, User-Agent, IP\r\n\r\nConfig (auto-detected):\r\n  ./caddy-analyzer.json        Local config\r\n  ~/.config/caddy-analyzer/config.json  Global config\r\n\r\nExamples:\r\n  caddy-analyze /var/log/caddy/access.log\r\n  caddy-analyze --detect /var/log/caddy/access.log\r\n  caddy-analyze --ip 10.0.0.0/8 access.log\r\n  caddy-analyze --5xx --no-bots access.log\r\n  caddy-analyze tail --ip 192.168.1.100 docker://caddy\r\n  caddy-analyze top ip --5xx -t 20 access.log\r\n  caddy-analyze diff base.log current.log\r\n\r\n"]
[7.429897, "o", "Usage:\r\n  caddy-analyze [flags] [source...]\r\n  caddy-analyze [command]\r\n\r\nAvailable Commands:\r\n  block       Block IP via iptables\r\n  config      Manage default log source and persistent configuration\r\n  diff        Compare two log files to detect RPS shifts, 5xx error spikes, and latency changes\r\n  guard       Auto-block malicious IPs in real time\r\n  help        Help about any command\r\n  tail        Stream and colorize Caddy access logs in real time\r\n  top         Quickly display top-N metrics for a specific dimension (path, ip, ua, status, bandwidth)\r\n  unban       Remove IP from firewall\r\n"]
[7.430125, "o", "\r\nFlags:\r\n      --2xx                  Filter 2xx status codes\r\n      --3xx                  Filter 3xx status codes\r\n      --4xx                  Filter 4xx status codes\r\n      --5xx                  Filter 5xx status codes\r\n      --bots-only            Include only automated bot traffic\r\n  -c, --compact              Compact output mode\r\n  -d, --detect               Detect suspicious activity (SQLi, XSS, scanners, etc.)\r\n  -e, --errors-only          Filter 5xx server errors only\r\n      --exclude-ip string    Exclude Remote IP\r\n  -F, --follow               Follow new logs in real time\r\n  -f, --format string        Output format: table, json, csv, html (default \"table\")\r\n      --from string          From (RFC3339 or relative: 5m, 1h, 2d)\r\n  -g, --grep string          Search pattern across URI, User-Agent, Remote IP\r\n  -h, --help                 help for caddy-analyze\r\n  -i, --interval string      Aggregation interval (e.g. 5m, 1h)\r\n      --ip string            Filter by Remote IP\r\n  -m, --method string        Filter by HTTP method\r\n  -n, --namespace string     Kubernetes namespace\r\n      --no-bots              Exclude automated bot and crawler traffic\r\n  -o, --output string        Write report to file instead of stdout\r\n  -p, --path string          Filter by path (glob: /api/*)\r\n      --slow string          Filter requests slower than duration (e.g. 500ms, 1s)\r\n  -s, --status stringArray   Filter by status code (e.g. -s 200,404)\r\n      --to string            To (RFC3339)\r\n  -t, --top int              Show top N (0 to disable) (default 10)\r\n  -v, --version              Version\r\n  -w, --watch                Live dashboard (RPS, top IP, status)\r\n\r\nUse \"caddy-analyze [command] --help\" for more information about a command.\r\n"]
